    tests: record four case-payload rows that already check (#2228)
    
    Four case-payload rows were listed as red in the corpus ledger, but main
    already checks them. This re-records them, so the scalar-range
    migration's remaining-work list no longer counts them. One more row that
    was never recorded is added, and it checks too.
    
    These rows are customers of **CANONICALIZE-SCALAR-RANGE-CONTRACTS**.
    Each was migrated from a payload suffix (`case X(v: T [lo..=hi])`) to a
    guarded data `requires` disjunct. A call inside the selected match arm
    relies on that disjunct, e.g. `take(lo, hi)` requiring `lo <= hi`. The
    ledger still showed the rejection recorded at `ccdb99ca2214`. At main
    `fea4cddc5c14`, these check:
    
    - `pass/cases/case_where_match`
    - `pass/cases/case_arm_pattern_names`
    - `pass/dependent/case_where_match_contributes`
    - `pass/dependent/case_where_generic_type_bound_coverage` (+ new row
    `..._coverage_exit`)
    
    No compiler code changes.
    
